# Payment Methods Policy for E-commerce Support

This sample policy describes payment methods supported by an e-commerce marketplace. Customers may pay using cash on delivery, bank card, debit card, credit card, linked wallet, bank transfer, promotional voucher balance, and other payment methods enabled by the platform at checkout. Available payment options may vary by seller, product type, delivery address, campaign, and buyer account status.

When a payment fails, the buyer should check card limits, wallet balance, bank authentication, one-time password confirmation, and network status. The platform may cancel unpaid orders after a timeout. For security, the support team should never ask customers to share full card numbers, passwords, OTP codes, or private banking credentials.

Refunds usually follow the original payment channel when possible. Cash on delivery refunds may be returned through wallet balance or another supported refund method. Promotional vouchers can be restored only when policy conditions allow it. Buyers can review payment status in order details and contact support when the transaction was charged but the order was not created.

This document provides repeated payment keywords for lexical search: payment methods, cash on delivery, credit card, debit card, bank transfer, wallet, voucher, refund to original payment method, failed payment, and order checkout support.
